    "result_text": "The full build passes (`BUILD SUCCESS`, all tests green).\n\n## Summary\n\nImplemented `contactPreference` on the owner response: `EMAIL` when an email is present, otherwise `PHONE`.\n\nTwo small, focused changes following the existing computed-field pattern:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a read-only `contactPreference` string property to the `Owner` schema (so the generated `OwnerDto` gains the field), documented alongside the other derived fields.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added `@Mapping(target = \"contactPreference\", expression = \"java(contactPreference(owner))\")` and a `contactPreference(Owner)` default method that returns `\"EMAIL\"` when the email is non-null and non-empty, else `\"PHONE\"`.\n\nThis reuses the established derivation approach already used for `displayName`, `initials`, `membershipNumber`, and `locality` \u2014 the mapper stays the single home for owner-to-DTO derivation, so no responder or entity code needed to change. Both new acceptance tests (`corePhoneWhenNoEmail`, `functionalityEmailWhenPresent`) and the rest of the suite pass.",
